invariant: INV-26
file: handshake_message.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: a raw or ca client outside PROFILE=cnsa2 takes -DCH_SUITE_AES_GCM, so a device image
  carries the AES suite and a traffic key path it never offers, and
  INV-26's second claim grows a build it does not describe. The Makefile
  refuses SUITE=aesgcm there; this #error is what refuses it for a tree
  with its own build system, and this edit removes it.

--- old
#if defined(CH_SUITE_AES_GCM) && !defined(CH_TRUST_WEBPKI) && !defined(CH_ROLE_SERVER) &&          \
    !defined(CH_PROFILE_CNSA2)
#error                                                                                             \
    "CH_SUITE_AES_GCM is refused for a raw or ca client: use TRUST=webpki, a server role or PROFILE=cnsa2"
#endif
--- new
